## Rules
- Unless the inputs say otherwise: storey height 3.0 m, exterior walls 300 mm, interior walls 120 mm, slabs 200 mm.
- One level per storey, named "Ground Floor", "First Floor", …
- Doors 900×2100, windows 1200×1200 with 900 sill, unless shown otherwise.
- Create spaces/rooms named from drawing text where available.
- Do not invent elements the inputs don't support.
- Metres, IFC4. Every element must be contained in a storey.
- List every assumption in `output/assumptions.md` (it is shown publicly next to the model).

## Deliver
- Route A (Revit): model with the Revit MCP, export IFC4 Reference View to `output/model.ifc`.
- Route B (Bonsai/IfcOpenShell): write the IFC directly to `output/model.ifc`.
- Then run `npm run tools -- validate {{ job.id }}` and fix any errors.
